# Chromium 152 V4L2 encoder on Linux: copy input frames into driver MMAP
# buffers instead of handing client memory to Venus as USERPTR.
#
# Applies to linux-mainline/out/chromium-v4l2-src/official-152 on top of
# chromium-152-v4l2-encode-linux.patch.
#
# The client frame is laid out for its own coded size (1920x1080 NV12 puts
# UV at row 1080); Venus reads the S_FMT layout (UV at row 1088, sizeimage
# bytes). USERPTR encoded the wrong chroma (WebCodecs PSNR 18-22 dB) and
# pinned memory past the frame; Iris2 then faulted in the SMMU and the
# firmware died. MMAP + libyuv copy/I420->NV12 gives 37-39 dB and no faults.
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
